From c1e34ec220ee9cc1dff43a11dcb3cb4e7cfab01b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <c@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:16:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Traction control wheel speeds from wired sensors or the CAN
 network (ABS)

Requested by Carlos (next firmware round, 01/11): wheel speeds by wire
and, if possible, also from CAN (car ABS or a module).
- new module TractionWheels, tcWheelSource:
  - wired: aux speed input 1 = front wheel, 2 = rear wheel, km/h from
    the tone ring teeth and the tire circumference
  - CAN: new targets Wheel speed FL/FR/RL/RR (km/h) for the custom CAN
    frames (any ABS whose frame layout is known) and the pro CAN
    slots; ftcan_target_e now 4 bits
  - axle speed = average of the wheels that work (CAN timeout 0.5 s)
- slip = driven / free axle (rear or front drive), not below tcMinSpeed,
  published as the WheelSlipRatio sensor that the existing traction
  control tables use (timing drop, ignition skip, throttle drop by slip
  x speed)
- optional traction control switch (tcSwitchPin)
- with no other speed sensor the free axle gives the vehicle speed
- CAN VSS and aux speed slip now register only when the sensor is free
  (no duplicate registration error)
- new alert sensor 'Wheel slip %' (gppwm channel 49); blend label offset
  49 -> 50
- live data: Wheel speed front/rear, Wheel slip %
- TunerStudio: Traction Control wheel speeds
- 4 new tests

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
